  "question": {
    "text": "An arithmetic progression is written in the following way\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bB7stDSups0-uIPe4AZasRrPBcAqCP8cz5i9_2KTLvs.original.fullsize.png\"><br />The sum of all the terms of the $10^{\\text {th }}$ row is_______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1505",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 2,5,11,20, \\ldots . . \\\\ & \\text { General term }=\\frac{3 n^2-3 n+4}{2} \\\\ & \\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{T}_{10}=\\frac{3(100)-3(10)+4}{2} \\\\ & \\quad= 137 \\\\ & 10 \\text { terms with c.d. }=3 \\\\ & \\text { sum }=\\frac{10}{2}(2(137)+9(3)) \\\\ &=1505\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
